# Local files only

Write code, tests, and docs in the project folders and stop there. The lead will put the work on GitHub later.

Do not commit, amend, create branches, push, add a remote, or open a pull request. Do not install or sign in to a git host in order to publish.

This replaces the branch, commit, and pull-request steps in the operating loop. Still run the tests and append `docs/PROGRESS.md`.

```bash
# BAD
git checkout -b feat/optimizer-core
git add backend/optimizer
git commit -m "Add the solver"
git push -u origin HEAD

# GOOD
# edit backend/optimizer/solver.py
# run pytest from /backend
# append docs/PROGRESS.md
# leave the files uncommitted
```
